          - name: annotate1
            mode: annotate
            title: Copyright
            text: The use of POP Fluid Solver tools is intended for your personal or professional creative projects, but must not be resold as-is (as .tox files, tool packs, templates, etc.). If you want to integrate these tools into a project or TouchDesigner file that will be sold to a client (installation, show pack, commercial template, client license, etc.), please contact me beforehand so we can agree on a proper license. Thanks for respecting this and supporting my work and future updates.
            position: [-375, 400]
            size: [382, 288]
            color: [0.5, 0.05, 0.05]
        annotations:
        - name: annotate1
          mode: annotate
          title: Forces and temperatures
          text: |2-







            No usage of forces or temperatures here. The forces applied in POP Fluid Solver are here only processed by the 3rd input.
          position: [-662, -167]
          size: [461, 206]
          color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
        - name: annotate2
          mode: annotate
          title: Mouse position
          text: |2-













            mouse_x and mouse_y allow to fit your mouse displacements according to your screen aspect ratio
          position: [-225, 375]
          size: [975, 310]
          color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
        - name: annotate3
          mode: annotate
          title: Geometry to "fluidify"
          text: Because we enabled life in POP_Fluid_Solver, we can move our input geometry, the positions will be updated. We use the mouse movement to translate the geometry in space
          position: [82, 45]
          size: [463, 269]
          color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
        - name: annotate4
          mode: annotate
          title: Geometry movement to forces
          text: "\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWe use the movement of the geometry as a forces input. The more we have points, to more powerful the force will be but also the more points, the more calculations.\n\nThanks to delete2 Thin parameter page, we keep 1000 points in the geometry. \nNo need to have a lot of points because we can still multiply the force calculated thanks to the POP_Fluid_Solver 'Geometry Forces Multiplier'."
          position: [500, -453]
          size: [419, 344]
          color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
        - name: annotate6
          mode: annotate
          title: 'Setup '
          text: |-
            Voxel_Grid_Init creates the calculations structure.

            1) Setup the 'Resolution' parameter. It represents how precise the simulation calculations will be

            2) Setup the Size of the simulation. You can observe the shape of this box thanks to the Geometry called 'box'

            Once you setup the Voxel_Grid_Init parameters, press the parameters 'Init' and then 'Start' to launch the simulation.
            Here you can press 0 to init and 1 to start.
          position: [-1100, -200]
          size: [382, 574]
          color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
